Package: rEGA
Type: Package
Title: Reliability Exploratory Graph Analysis (rEGA) and Nodal Variance Decomposition
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("C\u00e9sar", "Huerta-Huacchahuilca, César",
           email = "andrehuerta1411@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-8906-2678"))
  )
Description: Implements Reliability Exploratory Graph Analysis (rEGA), an autonomous
    network psychometrics framework that decomposes the Markov precision matrix via
    the Neumann-Markov resolvent operator. Eliminates L1 regularization bias through
    support-constrained maximum likelihood refitting, partitions nodal unit variance
    into within-community communality (h2), bridging variance (beta2), and Markov
    conditional uniqueness (psi2), and computes closed-form structural reliability
    coefficients (Network Gamma: Gamma_c and Gamma_t) alongside Graph Standard Errors
    of Measurement (SEM). Includes parallel bootstrap inference ('boot.rEGA'),
    attenuation-aware power planning, and Open Science cryptographic auditing.
